Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:41:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 004/105] perf: Triton W8A16 dense GEMV, hot-vocab draft head,
 adaptive logits buffer sizing

- Fp8LinearMethod.apply: opt-in Triton W8A16 GEMV (SGLANG_FP8_W8A16_GEMV=1) for M<=16
  replacing the cutlass W8A8 path that cost ~40us per call on skinny shapes
- qwen3_next: route the tiny in_proj_ba GEMM through the same Triton GEMV
  (SGLANG_GDN_BA_TRITON_GEMV=1); cuBLAS picked a ~39us kernel for a 0.5MB weight
- eagle_worker_v2.init_lm_head: dequantize FP8 target lm_head rows when building the
  hot-vocab (--speculative-token-map) draft head
- model_runner.max_decode_logits_rows: size the shared logits buffer for the widest
  adaptive candidate (fixes 16-vs-32-row assertion with --speculative-adaptive)

Measured (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next NVFP4, NEXTN steps 3, hot_32768 + FP8 shared_expert,attn,linear_attn):
agent-loop 174->244 t/s, code-edit 210->261, long-ctx 152->203, prose-en 131->163, prose-ja 117->165

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
